\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af48\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f48\fs20\kerning0\insrsid15404297 \hich\af48\dbch\af31505\loch\f48 
Briefly: 55-year-old man with relapsed/refractory nodular lymphocyte-predominant B-cell lymphoma, status post multiple prior lines of therapy and most recently receiving pola-ICE as bridging therapy to potential autologous stem-cell transplant versus CAR-
\hich\af48\dbch\af31505\loch\f48 T therapy, admitted with neutropenic fever, hypotension requiring vasopressor support, progressive \hich\af48\dbch\af31505\loch\f48 
odynophagia/dysphagia with throat pain, and diarrhea. Initial evaluation was notable for SARS-CoV-2 positivity (completed Paxlovid prior to/current admission), CT neck showing new supraglottic edema without drainable fluid collection, and CT abdomen/pelvi
\hich\af48\dbch\af31505\loch\f48 s showing colitis without obstruction. He received pegfilgrastim on 8/31, with persistent severe pancytopenia.\line \line 
He has remained on piperacillin-tazobactam 4.5 g IV every 12 hours since 9/8 for persistent neutropenic fever. He has also received IV f\hich\af48\dbch\af31505\loch\f48 
luconazole since 9/9, along with nystatin swish and swallow, for presumed Candida esophagitis in the setting of odynophagia and dysphagia, with a planned 14-day course. Despite clinical improvement, he had recurrent fever yesterday. He remains on room air
\hich\af48\dbch\af31505\loch\f48  with soft but stable blood pressures. Romiplostim was initiated 9/12 and filgrastim on 9/13, with subsequent improvement in WBC/ANC (currently ANC approximately 0.4)\line \line 
Infectious evaluation has been largely unrevealing to date. Blood cultures from \hich\af48\dbch\af31505\loch\f48 
9/11 and 9/13 remain without growth, and sputum culture showed pharyngeal flora only. Prior workup was negative for MRSA nares, group A Streptococcus, urinary Legionella and pneumococcal antigens, C. difficile, HHV-6, parvovirus B19, EBV PCR, and Aspergil
\hich\af48\dbch\af31505\loch\f48 
lus galactomannan. GI pathogen testing was positive for EPEC; norovirus was negative. SARS-CoV-2 remains positive on respiratory viral testing. CMV PCR was low-level positive at 68, and prior Fungitell was elevated at 167; repeat CMV/EBV PCR, beta-D-gluca
